basics for mysql:

login:
mysql -u username -p

create a database named unvstats:
CREATE DATABASE unvstats;

switch to it:
USE unvstats;

exit:
quit;

now to execute the data.sql and structure.sql:
mysql -u username -p unvstats < structure.sql
mysql -u username -p unvstats < data.sql

Existing databases: enable emoji in map names without recreating tables:
mysql -u username -p unvstats < upgrade_maps_utf8mb4.sql

Deploy the updated parser and web frontend, which use utf8mb4 connections,
then restart the parser. The NixOS module applies this migration automatically
for locally managed databases when unvstats-db-init runs. For an immediate
upgrade after rebuilding, run:
sudo systemctl restart unvstats-db-init.service unvstats-parser.service

Do not import structure.sql into an existing database: it drops tables.



